opening = md`Cloud Brain (\`cb4\`) is a set of Cloudflare Workers. Agents wrote almost all of it, through an issue loop that started on 2026-10-10. Nobody read every line. Now it is built, how do we understand it?

- Ask one question at a time.
- Answer each with a diagram drawn from the running system, not from memory.
- Every box links to that service's own reference, served by the Brain.
- Every line says where it comes from: the live **data**, the **docs**, or a guess.

*Draft: Tom to rewrite.*`
// %%
brainStatus = htl.html`<div style="font:13px system-ui;padding:.5em .8em;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);border-radius:6px">
  ${brainRaw.offline
    ? htl.html`<strong>Offline.</strong> Showing the copy saved ${brainRaw.fetchedAt.slice(0, 16).replace("T", " ")} UTC. (${brainRaw.offline})`
    : htl.html`<strong>Live.</strong> Read from <a href=${brainUrls(brainRaw.base).kernel} target="_blank">${brainRaw.base}</a> at ${brainRaw.fetchedAt.slice(11, 19)} UTC.`}
  ${brainTables.workers.length} Workers · ${brainTables.methods.length} methods · ${brainRows.edges.length} lines
  <span style="margin-left:1em">line styles:
    <svg width="40" height="8"><line x1="0" y1="4" x2="40" y2="4" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg> data
    <svg width="40" height="8"><line x1="0" y1="4" x2="40" y2="4" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 3"/></svg> docs
    <svg width="40" height="8"><line x1="0" y1="4" x2="40" y2="4" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="1.5 3"/></svg> guess
  </span>
</div>`
// %%
md`## 1. What runs?

- The Brain answers \`service.list\` to anyone: ${brainTables.workers.length - 1} Workers. The deployer answers for itself at its own address.
- Grouped by \`role\`, as the deployer records it.
- ${brainTables.workers.filter((w) => w.role === "recipe").length} of ${brainTables.workers.length} are a **recipe**: a service built from one notebook module.
- ↗ on a box opens that Worker's reference (\`getSource?part=reference\`).`
// %%
chapter_runs = diagramFor(chapters.runs, invalidation, brainRows)
// %%
md`## 2. Who deploys it?

- The relation is **deploys** (read backwards: *is deployed by*).
- No endpoint answers it. Both facts are sentences in the deployer's reference, so the lines are dashed:
  - "It distils module source to Worker code and deploys it."
  - "The installer deploys \`deployer_service\`, and nothing on the Brain can change it."
- So the chain is three steps deep: installer → deployer → every other Worker. Click the bar to unfold the ${brainTables.deploys.length - 1}.`
// %%
chapter_deploys = diagramFor(chapters.deploys, invalidation, brainRows)
// %%
md`## 3. Who can call it, and what does it call?

- y = the widest audience of any method, from each method's \`who\`: anyone, then other Workers, then the owner only.
- x = depth along **calls**, from \`getInfo\`'s \`calls\` joined to the Worker that owns each method. Solid lines: this is data.
- ${chapterCalls.excluded.length} Workers have no methods, so they have no row here (${chapterCalls.excluded.join(", ")}).
- ${chapterCalls.sccs.length ? `Dashed red: ${chapterCalls.sccs.map((s) => s.members.join(" ⇄ ")).join("; ")} call each other.` : "No Workers call each other."}`
// %%
chapter_calls = diagramFor(chapters.calls, invalidation, brainRows)
// %%
md`## 4. What does it touch?

- Each Worker declares resources (\`getInfo\`'s \`resources\`).
- The deployer's reference has a table from a declared resource to the binding it makes. The page reads that table live.
- y = depth along **binds**. Workers are at 0. What they bind is at 1. What brain-core binds is at 2.
- The Workers start folded. Each count is how many Workers bind that resource.`
// %%
chapter_binds = diagramFor(chapters.binds, invalidation, brainRows)
// %%
md`## 5. What do the docs not say?

- Declared resources with no row in the deployer's table: ${brainGaps.unmapped.length ? brainGaps.unmapped.map((d) => `\`${d}\``).join(", ") : "none"}.
- Lines by source: ${Object.entries(brainGaps.byProv).map(([k, n]) => `${n} ${k}`).join(", ")}.
- Not in any public answer: who deployed each version, version history, Cloudflare binding ids, the Fly machines.
- Each gap is a question to put to the service that owns it.`
// %%
md`## Explore

- Pick the levels yourself. The same model, any two axes.`
// %%
viewof explorePick = Inputs.form({
  y1: Inputs.select(Object.keys(exploreLevels), { label: "y", value: "role" }),
  y2: Inputs.select(["none", ...Object.keys(exploreLevels)], { label: "then y", value: "none" }),
  x: Inputs.select(["none", ...Object.keys(exploreLevels)], { label: "x", value: "calls (depth)" }),
  kinds: Inputs.checkbox(["worker", "cloudflare", "actor"], { label: "show", value: ["worker"] }),
  lines: Inputs.checkbox(["calls", "binds", "deploys"], { label: "lines", value: ["calls"] })
})
// %%
explore = {
  const p = explorePick;
  const lv = (k) => (k === "none" ? [] : [exploreLevels[k]]);
  const view = {
    name: `explore: ${p.y1}${p.y2 === "none" ? "" : " › " + p.y2} × ${p.x}`,
    y: [...lv(p.y1), ...lv(p.y2)], x: lv(p.x), xTitle: p.x === "none" ? "" : p.x, yTitle: "",
    kinds: p.kinds, drawRelations: p.lines, wrap: p.x === "none" ? 7 : 3
  };
  return diagramFor(view, invalidation, brainRows);
}
// %%
exploreLevels = ({
  "role": { col: "role" },
  "who can call": { col: "exposure", label: "exposure_name" },
  "test result": { col: "verified" },
  "deployed day": { col: "deployed_day" },
  "kind": { col: "kind" },
  "calls (depth)": { relation: "calls" },
  "binds (depth)": { relation: "binds" },
  "deploys (depth)": { relation: "deploys" }
})
// %%
md`### The model

- Loaded from public endpoints only. No token.
- Tables, then the SQL below, then the diagrams. The page draws from the same rows computed in JS (\`brainRowsOf\`), so the diagrams work without the SQL engine. \`test_brain_sql_matches_js\` checks the two agree.`
// %%
brainSqlText = htl.html`<pre style="font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap">-- nodes
${brainSql.nodes}

-- edges
${brainSql.edges}</pre>`
// %%
brainTablesView = htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">${["workers", "bindings", "deploys"].map((t) => htl.html`<div><strong>${t}</strong> · ${brainTables[t].length} rows${Inputs.table(brainTables[t], { rows: 8, layout: "auto" })}</div>`)}</div>`
// %%
brainRaw = {
  try {
    return await liveLib.loadBrain("cb4");
  } catch (e) {
    return { ...brainFixture, offline: e.message };
  }
}
// %%
brainTables = liveLib.tablesOf(brainRaw)
// %%
brainRows = liveLib.brainRowsOf(brainTables)
// %%
brainSql = liveLib.brainSql
// %%
brainUrls = liveLib.brainUrls
// %%
chapterCalls = engine.layout({ view: chapters.calls, ...brainRows })
// %%
brainGaps = {
  const mapped = new Set(brainTables.bindings.filter((b) => b.product).map((b) => b.declared));
  const unmapped = [...new Set(brainTables.resources.map((r) => r.declared))].filter((d) => !mapped.has(d)).sort();
  const byProv = {};
  for (const e of brainRows.edges) byProv[e.prov] = (byProv[e.prov] || 0) + 1;
  return { unmapped, byProv };
}
// %%
liveLib = {
/*@LIVE@*/
  return { brainUrls, parseBindings, productOf, loadBrain, tablesOf, brainSql, brainRowsOf };
}
// %%
chapters = {
/*@CHAPTERS@*/
  return chapters;
}
// %%
// cb4's public answers saved 2026-10-31, used when the page cannot reach cb4 and by the tests.
brainFixture = (/*@FIXTURE@*/)
// %%
test_brain_fixture = {
  const t = liveLib.tablesOf(brainFixture);
  const R = liveLib.brainRowsOf(t);
  if (t.workers.length !== 30) throw new Error("workers " + t.workers.length);
  const deploys = engine.layout({ view: chapters.deploys, ...R, folds: [] });
  if (deploys.rows.length !== 3) throw new Error("deploy steps " + deploys.rows.length);
  const calls = engine.layout({ view: chapters.calls, ...R });
  const cyc = calls.sccs.map((s) => s.members.join("+")).join(";");
  if (cyc !== "brain-x-fly+brain-x-loop") throw new Error("cycle " + cyc);
  const mapped = new Set(t.bindings.filter((b) => b.product).map((b) => b.declared));
  const gaps = [...new Set(t.resources.map((r) => r.declared))].filter((d) => !mapped.has(d)).sort().join(",");
  if (gaps !== "containers,workers") throw new Error("gaps " + gaps);
  return "fixture: 30 Workers, deploy chain 3 steps, fly ⇄ loop, gaps containers + workers";
}
// %%
// Needs sql.js (network).
test_brain_sql_matches_js = {
  const norm = (rows) => rows.map((r) => JSON.stringify(Object.keys(r).sort().map((k) => [k, r[k]]))).sort().join("\n");
  const sql = await runSql(brainTables, brainSql);
  for (const k of ["nodes", "edges"]) if (norm(sql[k]) !== norm(brainRows[k])) throw new Error(`${k}: SQL and brainRowsOf differ`);
  return `brainSql = brainRowsOf on ${brainRows.nodes.length} nodes and ${brainRows.edges.length} edges`;
}
// %%
md`## How to read these diagrams

The same engine on a small made-up web shop, one idea per step.`
